                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's bad. Horrendously so.\nImagine making a concept for a clicker game that is, as clicker games usually are, all about wasting people's time and waiting around. Then add a \"you have to click on new equipment as it drops to equip it\" and suddenly you're taking a passive game and making it active.\n\nIt's just the mousebutton-breaking, wrist-shattering shit that are clicker games and adding more tedious crap on top of it.\n\nAlso progression is really slow, so I guess they expected you to either pay up or spend 1000 hours on this game.\n\n*Edit:* I'm lowering the score by one. Because I was curious, I checked something. I went from Ivory 56 to Ivory 57, but looking at my damage, it went from 5.67 Qa down to 5.56 Qa. An upgrade lowers damage? Well f*ck you too.\n*Edit02:* And another -1. I reset and bought my way up, only for a skill to just disappear. A game-breaking bug. This is garbage.\n\n1/10. Don't touch this. Your still working mousebuttons will thank me later.",
